# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.metal.willow), on the willow.
#
# The Metal driver of this port (src/redwoodmetal.m, built for redwood's Adreno 642L) on the willow's
# Adreno 610, for the first time. Nothing in it names the GPU: the compiler library
# (tools/mesa/air/air_metal.c) opens freedreno through the same RedwoodGPU client Mesa's OpenGL ES
# does, and freedreno takes the model from the kernel's CHIP_ID. The window server draws with the same
# GPU meanwhile (gpu=1, GL=1).
#
# The wait is cpu_test's and not rwtouch's: on the willow rwtouch did not come back from opening
# /dev/redwood-touch (rc.jobs.gltest.willow). By then SpringBoard is up and the GPU is the window
# server's as well.
/redwood/bin/cpu_test 40
#
# 1. Does the driver load, is it taken by Metal (steps 4 and 5, MTLAddDevice,
#    MTLCreateSystemDefaultDevice), and how many of AV1SW.metallib's functions compile for the A610.
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test
#
# 2. The kernels that bind only buffers and are known to end (rc.jobs.metalcompute): each its own
#    process, so a crash costs one line.
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib MetalFaceMask_InitMinMax
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib MetalFaceMask_CalcCubeInputScaling
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib MetalFaceMask_InitSpanTable
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib MetalFaceMask_PropogateAssociations
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib fbs_bistochastize_init
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib fbs_pcg_iter2
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib fbs_pcg_iter3
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib image_calcminmax0
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib image_calcminmax2
#
# 3. One triangle with one of Apple's own fragment shaders (clearFragment20), whose pixels have a
#    reference from softpipe (rc.jobs.metaldraw).
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --draw /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
